<!--
  The dashboard model and quick access (batch B12): the names of the Home shortcuts (Quick access and
  Setting tiles), the shortcut groups, what a tile shows as its value, how a tile is announced to a
  screen reader, the names of the dashboard widget types and the shipped example's titles, and the
  default names of the saved layout slots. The English must stay exactly what the source said before
  the batch (G1, G2; tests/l10n/characterization/DashboardModelEnglishTest.java pins every shortcut).

  Stored values stay English: a widget's saved title, an export and an import keep the English text,
  and an owner's own title is shown as typed. Only a title that is still its type's default (or one of
  the shipped example's titles, or a default slot name) is shown through these entries.

  Shortcut names are a narrow-label ladder: the full name (Quick access buttons, their tooltips, the
  shortcut picker, and the screen-reader name of both a Quick access button and a Setting tile) and a
  _short rung (the single-line label of a Setting tile, about 90 dp wide at 12.5 sp). In English both
  rungs are the same text; translate both, and make the short one shorter where the full name would
  not fit.

  A Quick access button is at least 72 dp wide with 4 dp padding on each side, so its name has 64 dp
  per line at 12 sp (volt:max="64dp@12sp" on every full name; at the smallest app text size the
  column narrows with the text, to about 61 dp at 12 sp). The name may wrap onto two lines; one that
  would take three is shrunk to 10 sp. A single word must fit one line: a wider word is broken in the
  middle (the English "Experimental", "preferences" and "permissions", 66 to 74 dp at 12 sp, escape
  that only because their names then run to three lines and shrink). The width check measures the
  whole name on one line, so a name over the budget can still be right when it wraps between words
  into two lines.

  Tile announcements (the _desc_ entries) are joined in a fixed order after the shortcut's name:
  name, then the value, then why it is muted, then "toggle" or "open". Each entry carries its own
  separator (", ") so a language with another list separator can change it.
-->
<resources xmlns:volt="https://volt.jjricks.com/ns/l10n"
    xmlns:xliff="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">

